      "problem": "Find the value of  $(\\sqrt{36}+16)÷(-7-4).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt{36}+16)÷(-7-4) & = \\\\ (\\sqrt{36}+16)÷(-11) & = \\\\ (\\sqrt{6\\cdot 6}+16)÷(-11) & = \\\\ (\\sqrt{{6}^{2}}+16)÷(-11) & = \\\\ (6+16)÷(-11) & = \\\\ 22÷(-11) & = \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
